            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0451" n="442" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3768: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tours</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-14T07:00:00+01:00">June 14, 1940—7
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 14—3:54 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. I was telephoned at 5:30 this morning that French Government is proceeding to
                    Bordeaux region today. I am now en route to see Reynaud some 70 kilometers
                    distant and will telegraph as soon as possible thereafter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
